// t_36492ad8 commit 1.  A NAME USED AND THEN DECLARED LATER IN THE SAME
// LEXICAL SCOPE is refused - "error C1002: the name X is already defined" -
// and the refusal does NOT depend on reachability, so it is not the deferred
// C1008 class.  Every other arrangement is legal, measured over nine probes
// on sce-cgc 475 (codex): use outer / declare inner, use inner / declare
// outer, two sibling blocks, and file-scope-later all compile.
//
// THE KEY IS THE SCOPE INSTANCE.  Recording the unresolved use against the
// FUNCTION would refuse three of those legal shapes; recording it against the
// scope DEPTH cannot tell two sibling blocks apart.
//
// ACCEPT: use INNER, declare OUTER.  Legal.
float4 unused(float4 t) { { float4 q = missing(t); } float missing; return t; }
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return t; }
